timeline.body:
@andreidan , thanks for replying! I will be of course not merging this until we clarify how it works on the cloud.

> I've quickly tested this and I think it might not work if the repository has snapshots (or maybe cloud has a special handling of the found-snapshots repo).

The integration test of this PR does have a snapshot in it when it becomes corrupt. And re-registering the repository then resets the corrupt flag, and the test continues to actually delete the snapshot and it does so successfully. However, it's of course not on the cloud. So for the moment, I believe it may be something in the cloud or some special handling of `found-snapshots` repo; btw, I'm not an expert yet here. If you can also give me guidance, I can also try testing the cloud scenario. But feel free to do it yourself and let me know of any issues, thanks!

